 {"id":"REVIEW-1","title":"SECURITY: the dashboard ships a default API key in source, binds 0.0.0.0, and prints the key to stdout","status":"complete","priority":"P0","complexity":1,"depends_on":[],"blocks":[],"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"reasoning":"Third-party hands-on review, reproduced on a scratch instance I started myself (port 4701, since stopped). src/dashboard/main.py:37 is `API_KEY = os.getenv(\"PTP_API_KEY\", \"ptp-secret-key-12345\")` \u2014 a committed default. REPRODUCED: `curl .../status` -> HTTP 401 unauthenticated, but `curl -H 'X-API-Key: ptp-secret-key-12345' .../status` -> HTTP 200 (and /metrics -> 200). The docstring 8 lines above (:46-53) claims the opposite: '...which leaves authenticated calls at 401 rather than falling back to a committed default.' Code contradicts its own comment. Three compounding factors: (1) default bind is 0.0.0.0 (`host = os.getenv(\"PTP_DASHBOARD_HOST\", \"0.0.0.0\")`, :506-509); (2) startup prints the key to stdout (`print(f\"API Key: {API_KEY}\")`, :512) so it lands in logs and scrollback; (3) the key unlocks POST /control/start, /control/stop, /control/pause, /control/command \u2014 remote control of a running agent. THE REPO IS PUBLIC (github.com/wojons/ai_plays_poke), so the default credential is public. Done-when: API_KEY has no default (fail closed when PTP_API_KEY is unset), PTP_DASHBOARD_HOST defaults to 127.0.0.1, and the key is not printed. Estimated 45 min total.","created_at":"2026-09-27T16:45:38.639400+00:00","completed_at":"2026-09-27 20:10:00","commit_hash":"692cddd","worker_model":"glm-5.3-flash","worker_provider":"xkiro"}
